Z||000000||Zorba||10-03-2000||04:02 AM||||If you have a 68 block/engine, how do you go about the emissions issue in your state and what can be done so your new v8 fiero can pass with flywing colors? In the state of utah you can receive a "waver" after demonstrating that you have attempted at least $200 towards making the car cleaner.<BR>You need an exemption each year. I believe 67 and older engines are emissions exempt here.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-03-2000||07:26 AM||||How about a catilitic(sp?) converter and an electronic ignition (H.E.I.). Those items would easily exceed $200 each if professionally installed.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000002||theogre||10-03-2000||08:54 AM||||Is this a change you are plannig or one already done? If that 67 block is original it may not like running w/o lead in the gas. Has a nasty habbit of chewing the valves.<P>Usually emissions are regulated by year of the car. They don't care what motor is in it. It has to pass what ever is set for that year car.<P>Mostly you're going to need a <I>really</I> good tuneup. You'll need a catalyst if they look for it. You may need one anyway just to pass the gas analyzer. If the thing runs very rich you'll have trouble with the catalyst. The cat is intended to clean up a motor that's running right. Too rich and it will cook like hell. Can get so hot it glows.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
